Write a function lcm32 that takes two unsigned 32-bit numbers a and b and returns their least common multiple, computed as a divided by gcd(a, b), times b. When a or b is 0 the result is 0. Write and use a helper function gcd(a, b) that returns the greatest common divisor by repeated remainders (gcd(a, 0) = a). Unsigned 32-bit arithmetic wraps around modulo 2^32 (it never traps).
